WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.186 --> 00:00:01.329
- Good morning Believe Nation.

00:00:01.329 --> 00:00:03.213
Todays message is

00:00:03.213 --> 00:00:04.326
rest.

00:00:04.326 --> 00:00:05.934
Over to you Rick Warren.

00:00:05.934 --> 00:00:08.066
(rooster crowing)

00:00:08.066 --> 00:00:11.009
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:11.009 --> 00:00:13.080
♫ Entspresso keeps me going

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:16.580
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:17.441 --> 00:00:19.121
- I take Monday off.

00:00:19.121 --> 00:00:20.136
Monday is my Sabbath.

00:00:20.136 --> 00:00:21.261
I don't like taking Monday off

00:00:21.261 --> 00:00:23.480
because I don't like feeling
that bad on my day off.

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:25.707
(chuckles)

00:00:25.707 --> 00:00:28.477
But I find that I need to to recharge

00:00:28.477 --> 00:00:31.689
and on Mondays, I am dead to the world.

00:00:31.689 --> 00:00:33.339
I do not take calls.

00:00:33.339 --> 00:00:34.711
I do not read email.

00:00:34.711 --> 00:00:37.055
I do not take text messages.

00:00:37.055 --> 00:00:39.867
I sleep in, I get up,
I play around the house

00:00:39.867 --> 00:00:41.331
I go to lunch with my wife.

00:00:41.331 --> 00:00:43.277
We relax in the afternoon

00:00:43.277 --> 00:00:46.032
and Monday evenings we do
family night with our families.

00:00:46.032 --> 00:00:49.905
We now have grandkids that are involved.

00:00:49.905 --> 00:00:51.632
And we've kept that religiously.

00:00:51.632 --> 00:00:53.680
We've kept that faithfully over the years

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:55.889
and it has kept me from burning out

00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:57.889
under enormous pressure.

00:01:00.702 --> 00:01:02.489
How would you like to pastor a church

00:01:02.489 --> 00:01:05.507
where you move the
church building 79 times

00:01:05.507 --> 00:01:07.204
in the first 13 years?

00:01:07.204 --> 00:01:08.037
I did.

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:12.692
Because land was so expensive

00:01:12.692 --> 00:01:16.450
we used 79 different facilities
in the first 13 years.

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:18.932
Some weeks, I'd be in
five different buildings.

00:01:18.932 --> 00:01:20.972
Laguna Hills High School
for Sunday morning.

00:01:20.972 --> 00:01:23.232
El Toro High School Sunday evening.

00:01:23.232 --> 00:01:24.630
A bank building for Wednesday.

00:01:24.630 --> 00:01:25.805
Another one on Thursday.

00:01:25.805 --> 00:01:27.568
A Saturday night service at another school

00:01:27.568 --> 00:01:28.517
and on and on.

00:01:28.517 --> 00:01:30.093
We said, "We're the church
if you can figure out

00:01:30.093 --> 00:01:31.670
"where we are this week, you get to come."

00:01:31.670 --> 00:01:33.799
(congregation laughs)

00:01:33.799 --> 00:01:34.647
We said, "We only want our church

00:01:34.647 --> 00:01:35.878
"for really intelligent people

00:01:35.878 --> 00:01:37.817
"so we keep changing the location."

00:01:37.817 --> 00:01:39.689
(congregation laughs)

00:01:39.689 --> 00:01:42.521
But that was a lot of frustration.

00:01:42.521 --> 00:01:44.946
And I can tell you I
have learned to handle

00:01:44.946 --> 00:01:47.113
enormous amounts of stress

00:01:48.229 --> 00:01:51.203
and enormous amounts of tension.

00:01:51.203 --> 00:01:52.338
But I could not do it

00:01:52.338 --> 00:01:54.100
if I didn't rest my body.

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:55.358
If I didn't take my day off.

00:01:55.358 --> 00:01:57.457
If I didn't, and don't
call it your day off.

00:01:57.457 --> 00:01:58.614
Call it your sabbath.

00:01:58.614 --> 00:01:59.794
Call it your day off, you'll fill it

00:01:59.794 --> 00:02:01.982
with your honey-do list.

00:02:01.982 --> 00:02:02.952
All the stuff that couldn't get done

00:02:02.952 --> 00:02:04.719
you try to use it to
catch up on other stuff.

00:02:04.719 --> 00:02:07.071
No, it is a day of rest, relaxation

00:02:07.071 --> 00:02:10.712
relationships, restoration emotionally.

00:02:10.712 --> 00:02:12.951
So you need to rest your body.

00:02:12.951 --> 00:02:14.994
- So this is a really
interesting one for me

00:02:14.994 --> 00:02:17.287
because my default is to work.

00:02:17.287 --> 00:02:18.307
I like to work.

00:02:18.307 --> 00:02:21.224
I gain calm and clarity in my work.

00:02:23.328 --> 00:02:24.673
Sometimes when I rest too much

00:02:24.673 --> 00:02:26.209
like if I go on a beachy vacation

00:02:26.209 --> 00:02:27.955
I get really antsy and frustrated.

00:02:27.955 --> 00:02:28.954
I want to work.

00:02:28.954 --> 00:02:30.265
I hate just sitting down

00:02:30.265 --> 00:02:32.941
and being on a beach for a week.

00:02:32.941 --> 00:02:34.072
I can handle like one day

00:02:34.072 --> 00:02:36.509
but after that, I want to do something.

00:02:36.509 --> 00:02:39.416
You know, if Nina's
away for whatever reason

00:02:39.416 --> 00:02:40.622
my default is to work.

00:02:40.622 --> 00:02:42.078
I'm going to go back and work on projects

00:02:42.078 --> 00:02:44.148
because it fills me up and makes me happy.

00:02:44.148 --> 00:02:46.335
So this is a harder one for me to answer.

00:02:46.335 --> 00:02:49.520
I think the best thing
that I can give you guys

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:50.600
as my advice

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:52.912
is to listen to your body.

00:02:52.912 --> 00:02:56.271
Where some days you may need to rest more.

00:02:56.271 --> 00:02:57.765
You know, if you're feeling sick

00:02:57.765 --> 00:02:59.400
or life is overwhelming

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:00.898
maybe you need to rest more.

00:03:00.898 --> 00:03:03.025
And other days, you're able to work more.

00:03:03.025 --> 00:03:03.985
You're able to grind it out.

00:03:03.985 --> 00:03:05.045
You're able to hustle.

00:03:05.045 --> 00:03:06.483
I'm in the camp that believes

00:03:06.483 --> 00:03:09.319
that if you are itching for a vacation

00:03:09.319 --> 00:03:11.234
if you like, can't wait to get away

00:03:11.234 --> 00:03:12.732
to get on that vacation

00:03:12.732 --> 00:03:15.022
then something is wrong in your life.

00:03:15.022 --> 00:03:16.240
Vacations can add a lot.

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:18.588
The travel can give
you lots of great ideas

00:03:18.588 --> 00:03:19.445
can help you grow

00:03:19.445 --> 00:03:20.403
and that's a different thing.

00:03:20.403 --> 00:03:23.155
But if you're itching
to get away to escape

00:03:23.155 --> 00:03:25.853
to just relax and wind down

00:03:25.853 --> 00:03:28.253
I feel like there's
something wrong in your life.

00:03:28.253 --> 00:03:29.515
That's my belief.

00:03:29.515 --> 00:03:32.030
And instead of once or twice a year

00:03:32.030 --> 00:03:34.768
escaping from your life
to go do something else

00:03:34.768 --> 00:03:36.259
make your life better.

00:03:36.259 --> 00:03:37.305
That's my view.

00:03:37.305 --> 00:03:38.574
If you're thinking about
how you're spending

00:03:38.574 --> 00:03:40.039
your spare time or your free time

00:03:40.039 --> 00:03:41.594
are you spending it in escapism?

00:03:41.594 --> 00:03:44.460
Are you spending it
watching Big Brother 18

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:46.451
or some reality TV show

00:03:46.451 --> 00:03:48.495
or stupid cats fighting each other

00:03:48.495 --> 00:03:49.670
or whatever it is?

00:03:49.670 --> 00:03:51.318
That's escapism, that's super easy.

00:03:51.318 --> 00:03:52.151
That's what most people will do.

00:03:52.151 --> 00:03:53.282
They come home and sit on the couch

00:03:53.282 --> 00:03:55.813
and plop down and just
escape from their life

00:03:55.813 --> 00:03:57.513
by being entertained

00:03:57.513 --> 00:03:59.398
or watching the misery
of other peoples lives

00:03:59.398 --> 00:04:01.092
which makes them feel
better about themselves.

00:04:01.092 --> 00:04:02.865
Is that how you're spending
your time, escapism?

00:04:02.865 --> 00:04:05.347
Or are you spending your time
trying to grow and get better?

00:04:05.347 --> 00:04:07.223
Like, are you spending
time watching videos?

00:04:07.223 --> 00:04:08.433
Are you spending time reading a book?

00:04:08.433 --> 00:04:09.877
Are you spending time learning techniques

00:04:09.877 --> 00:04:11.677
about your industry?

00:04:11.677 --> 00:04:12.977
Are you spending time
learning and growing?

00:04:12.977 --> 00:04:14.820
If you are unhappy with your life

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:16.943
audit how you're spending your extra time.

00:04:16.943 --> 00:04:19.496
Are you spending your time
escaping the life that you hate

00:04:19.496 --> 00:04:22.066
or are you spending your
time growing and building

00:04:22.066 --> 00:04:24.291
so that you can build a
better life for yourself?

00:04:24.291 --> 00:04:25.737
And for me, a lot of times vacation

00:04:25.737 --> 00:04:29.355
most of the time falls into
that category of escapism.

00:04:29.355 --> 00:04:31.629
Like I hate my life, I hate what I'm doing

00:04:31.629 --> 00:04:33.012
so I need to get away from it

00:04:33.012 --> 00:04:35.586
and then I'll come back
and I'll suffer some more

00:04:35.586 --> 00:04:36.879
until my next vacation.

00:04:36.879 --> 00:04:37.712
But that sucks.

00:04:37.712 --> 00:04:39.110
Most people live for the
evenings and weekends

00:04:39.110 --> 00:04:39.943
and vacations

00:04:39.943 --> 00:04:42.650
as opposed to actually
enjoying and being fulfilled

00:04:42.650 --> 00:04:45.090
in the work that you're doing every day.

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:47.828
And so the "rest" one is
a little bit harder for me

00:04:47.828 --> 00:04:50.601
again, because I default to work.

00:04:50.601 --> 00:04:52.163
And maybe that will change when I'm older.

00:04:52.163 --> 00:04:55.496
Maybe I'll feel like I need to rest more

00:04:56.468 --> 00:04:59.282
but I also feel like I need
to spend time with my wife.

00:04:59.282 --> 00:05:00.750
I need to spend time with my son.

00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:02.485
I need to spend time with my family.

00:05:02.485 --> 00:05:04.534
And things are always kind of
fighting against each other.

00:05:04.534 --> 00:05:06.820
I need to balance my
schedule to make it work

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:08.581
because I'm not just an entrepreneur

00:05:08.581 --> 00:05:10.312
and only focus on business.

00:05:10.312 --> 00:05:13.334
I also want to be a successful father

00:05:13.334 --> 00:05:14.658
and a successful husband

00:05:14.658 --> 00:05:15.692
and a successful family man.

00:05:15.692 --> 00:05:16.822
And so part of what I do daily

00:05:16.822 --> 00:05:19.690
is look at my goals of those categories.

00:05:19.690 --> 00:05:22.891
Of family man, leader,
and my own personal health

00:05:22.891 --> 00:05:23.829
and making sure I'm spending time

00:05:23.829 --> 00:05:25.680
on all three of those every day.

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:29.420
So I don't know that my advice
would be to rest once a week

00:05:29.420 --> 00:05:31.691
but I would say listen to your body.

00:05:31.691 --> 00:05:34.092
And do what's right for you.

00:05:34.092 --> 00:05:36.266
The question of the day today then is

00:05:36.266 --> 00:05:37.869
how important is rest for you?

00:05:37.869 --> 00:05:38.849
I'm curious.

00:05:38.849 --> 00:05:40.341
How much do you rest?

00:05:40.341 --> 00:05:41.674
Is it important?

00:05:42.512 --> 00:05:44.060
Give me some advice.

00:05:44.060 --> 00:05:45.253
Share with Believe Nation.

00:05:45.253 --> 00:05:47.245
I'm super curious to hear
what you have to say.

00:05:47.245 --> 00:05:48.714
Leave it down in the comments below

00:05:48.714 --> 00:05:50.234
and we'll join in the discussion.

00:05:50.234 --> 00:05:52.154
I also want to give a quick
shout-out to Dutch Martin.

00:05:52.154 --> 00:05:53.302
Dutch, thank you so much for picking

00:05:53.302 --> 00:05:55.200
up a copy of my book, Your One Word

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:57.443
it really, really,
really means a lot to me

00:05:57.443 --> 00:05:58.960
and I hope you're enjoying it.

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:00.433
Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:06:00.433 --> 00:06:01.525
I believe in you.

00:06:01.525 --> 00:06:03.411
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:06:03.411 --> 00:06:05.353
and whatever your one word is.

00:06:05.353 --> 00:06:06.655
And I'll see you again tomorrow morning

00:06:06.655 --> 00:06:08.851
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:06:08.851 --> 00:06:11.869
♫ I wake up every morning

00:06:11.869 --> 00:06:15.022
